  actor: jgstern_agent  # 338a
  clock: 2  # 338a
  nonce: 338a  # 338a
  message: "PHASE 0 RE-VERIFICATION AT TIP, 2026-08-25, dev e41a655d6d. REPRODUCES,\nunchanged, on this item's own filed pair:\n\n    http.Get(u)   [package-qualified FREE FUNCTION] -> cc=method\n    c.Get(u)      [value-receiver METHOD]           -> cc=method\n    os.Getwd()    [package-qualified free function] -> cc=method\n    f.Close()     [method on typed local]           -> cc=method\n\ngo.py does now emit call_construct='function' at three sites (~2998, ~3044,\n~3105), but none of them fires for a call into an UNRESOLVED external package\n-- which is the population the io-boundary F3 gate reads. The field is still\nconstant across the construct distinction it exists to record.\n\nPhase 6 (recall), owner-gated. Status unchanged: violated."  # 338a
- op: discuss  # 320f
  at: '2026-08-27T15:58:23Z'  # 320f
  by: agent  # 320f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 320f
  clock: 3  # 320f
  nonce: 320f  # 320f
  message: "CORPUS-WIDE EVIDENCE for this item, from the 2026-08-27 fundamental concept\naudit of call_construct (write-up:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-call_construct_08272026.md).\n\nThis item's statement -- \"the field records the SYNTAX, not the construct its\nname promises\" -- is now measured beyond Go, on 42 cached surveys\n(lutuh_scope_08242026), 261,365 stamped edges, 19 languages.\n\n1. call_construct is NOT derivable from the callee's Symbol.kind: over\n   261,277 resolved call edges they disagree 85.8% of the time. The single\n   largest honest-disagreement cell is function -> method at 19,611 edges\n   (the converse of this item's Go case), plus method -> function at 471.\n   So the confusion is bidirectional and not Go-specific.\n\n2. In the population where it actually costs something -- external callees\n   whose (module, name) matches an io_primitives row, so the catalogue's own\n   declared kind is available as ground truth -- call_construct disagrees\n   with that declared kind 71.8% of the time (3,355 of 4,672). The\n   method -> function cell there is 867 edges, which is this item's defect\n   measured against the catalogue rather than against a fixture.\n\n3. Scope note: the 2,434 remote -> function and 54 application -> function\n   cells in the same measurement are a DIFFERENT defect (erlang/haskell\n   stamping locality and synonym words on a construct key) and are filed\n   separately as WI-kohig. They are not part of this item.\n\nNO STATUS CHANGE PROPOSED. The item reproduces; this is evidence for sizing,\nnot a closure. The audit also filed INV-pimir for the consumer-side join that\nmakes this field's inaccuracy actionable, and that item cites this one as\nrelated-not-duplicate."  # 320f
- op: discuss  # 6632
  at: '2026-09-07T12:24:58Z'  # 6632
  by: agent  # 6632
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6632
  clock: 4  # 6632
  nonce: '6632'  # 6632
  message: "RE-VERIFIED AT TIP 2026-09-07 (dev ce34cc86b7) AND SIZED AT THE CONSUMER FOR THE FIRST TIME. Reporting only -- NO status change (it reproduces and stays violated), no re-prioritisation, no fix attempted. Instruments: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/tanom_recheck_09072026/ (fx/, probe.py, size.py, spotcheck.txt).\n\nIT REPRODUCES, on this item's own filed pairs, production analyze_go, one file, one run:\n    http.Get(u)     PACKAGE-QUALIFIED FREE FUNCTION -> go:net/http:0-0:Get:unresolved   cc=method\n    os.ReadFile(p)  PACKAGE-QUALIFIED FREE FUNCTION -> go:os:0-0:ReadFile:unresolved    cc=method\n    os.Getwd()      PACKAGE-QUALIFIED FREE FUNCTION -> go:os:0-0:Getwd:unresolved       cc=method\n    c.Get(u)        VALUE-RECEIVER METHOD           -> go:net/http:0-0:Get:unresolved   cc=method  receiver=external\n    f.Close()       METHOD on a typed local         -> go:os:0-0:Close:unresolved       cc=method  receiver=external\n    helper(x)       in-file free function           -> resolved first-party             cc=function\nUnchanged from the 2026-08-25 entry, including that `receiver` presence is the only discriminator and this item already showed it is not a safe one.\n\nTHE SIZING THIS ITEM ASKED FOR AND NEVER HAD (\"it would change a field several consumers read and HAS NOT BEEN SIZED\"). Measured on alertmanager (261 .go files, 14,331 go call edges, with an input positive control so a missing path could not read as \"no cost\" -- the first attempt pointed at a repository that is not in the corpus and returned 0 edges, which is exactly the manufactured absence LIVE rule 6 names):\n\n    7,162  module slot FILLED, cc=method   <- the gate NEVER reads call_construct here\n    4,936  resolved first-party            <- the gate is not reached\n    2,229  NO module slot, cc=method       <- the only edges whose construct the gate reads\n        4  module slot FILLED, cc=function\n\nTHE CONSUMER COST IS ZERO ON THIS REPOSITORY, and the mechanism is structural rather than lucky. io-boundary reads `call_construct` ONLY on the no-module path (the same fact that closed INV-gijis today). A PACKAGE-QUALIFIED call always takes its module slot from the import, so the shape this item is about -- a free function stamped `method` -- never reaches the branch where the constant field could mislead. Of the 2,229 edges that DO reach it, 67 carry a name that is a FUNCTION-kind row only, which is the shape that could have cost a wrong refusal; reading all 67 at source shows their receivers are local VALUES (`clock.Now()` in a bench test, `am.WriteString(...)`, `f.Stat()`, `routingCmd.Command(...)`, `tempFile.Open()`), i.e. genuine method calls, correctly stamped, correctly refused against a function-kind row. That is INV-tapat working, not this defect biting.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT CHANGE. The item's factual claim is intact and its title is accurate: the field records the SYNTAX, not the construct. What is now measured is that its stated consequence is entirely FORWARD-LOOKING -- \"any FUTURE predicate keyed on call_construct to separate a function row from a method row is keyed on a constant and cannot work\" -- and costs nothing at today's consumer. That matches this item's own text (\"the gate is still correct ... which is a different input\") and the 2026-08-27 concept audit's refusal to propose a status change. So the decision this item needs is about VOCABULARY DEBT, not about a live defect, and it should be priced that way.\n\nNOT ESTABLISHED: one Go repository. gocryptfs, prometheus and the rest of the go cohort were not run, and a repository with vendored or unresolvable imports could plausibly produce package-qualified calls WITHOUT a module slot -- the one shape that would make this cost something. Sizing that is the next step if anyone wants to spend on this item; it needs an AST-level split of the 2,229 (is the receiver an imported package name or a value?), which this instrument does not do."  # 6632
- op: discuss  # 1352
  at: '2026-09-09T07:52:48Z'  # 1352
  by: agent  # 1352
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1352
  clock: 5  # 1352
  nonce: '1352'  # 1352
  message: "SIZED ACROSS THE GO COHORT 2026-09-09. NO STATUS CHANGE: it reproduces, it stays violated, and \"costs nothing today\" is not a satisfied invariant. Instruments: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/tanom_sizing_09092026/ (split.py, control_check.py, cohort.sh, RESULT.md, INSTRUMENT_DEFECTS.md).\n\nTHIS ANSWERS THE QUESTION THIS ITEM ASKED AND ITS OWN INSTRUMENT COULD NOT. The 2026-09-07 entry sized the cost at zero on ONE repository and named what was missing: \"a repository with vendored or unresolvable imports could plausibly produce package-qualified calls WITHOUT a module slot -- the one shape that would make this cost something ... it needs an AST-level split of the 2,229 (is the receiver an imported package name or a value?)\". That split now exists.\n\nRESULT: the shape does not occur. 14 Go repositories, 10 of them carrying a vendor/ tree, 72,396 unresolved cc=method call edges with NO module slot -- the only population io-boundary ever reads this field for, since F3 consults it exclusively on the no-module path:\n\n    repo                noModuleMethod  COSTLY      repo              noModuleMethod  COSTLY\n    alertmanager                  2229       0      cert-manager                7503       0\n    gvisor-tap-vsock               288       0      argo-cd                    18147       0\n    buildah                       1697       0      compose-go                   121       0\n    distribution                  1849       0      moby                       11440       0\n    docker-cli                    3752       0      beads                       9254       0\n    containerd                    8581       0      keda                        3639       0\n    containers-storage            1416       0      coredns                     2480       0\n    TOTAL                                                                     72,396       0\n\nThe zero is STRUCTURAL, not lucky: a package qualifier always names an import in the file's own import block, so the module slot is always fillable, and only value receivers reach the no-module branch. Accounting is complete rather than residual -- alertmanager's 2,229 = 1,817 value + 392 chained + 173 field + 24 unrecoverable + 5 ambiguous + 0 package-qualified. The unknown cell is 29/2,229 = 1.3% and is the BOUND on the zero, not engineered away.\n\nFOUR INSTRUMENT DEFECTS, EVERY ONE BIASED TOWARD \"THIS IS A LIVE DEFECT\", all found by reading flagged sites at source rather than publishing the count:\n1. LINE COLLISION -- an edge carries a line, not a column, and `attribute.String(\"...\", a.Fingerprint().String())` emits two `String` edges on one line. Cost: 5 of the first 6 hits. This is WI-divin (filed hours earlier today) biting a second consumer.\n2. A FORWARD LINE WINDOW added to cut an 18% \"unrecoverable\" rate -- it MANUFACTURED both surviving hits (the edge at notify_test.go:502 is `err.Error()`; the window reached line 504's `require.Error`). Cost: 100% of the finding that would have been published. Reverted to own-line; the unrecoverable rate is reported as a bound instead.\n3. FIELD/PACKAGE NAME COLLISION -- `cp.time.Sub(prev)` and `tc.encoding.NewEncoder()` are methods on struct FIELDS whose names collide with imports. Cost: the last 2 hits in the cohort. The tell was readable: `time.Sub` is not a free function in Go at all.\n4. THE CONTROL'S OWN DENOMINATOR was impure -- it assumed module-FILLED implies package-qualified and thresholded the rate at 50%, so coredns \"failed\" at 40.4%. Reading twelve coredns sites shows go.py fills the slot from the receiver's inferred TYPE too (`e.Client.Delete`, `r.Req.Copy`, `time.Now().Unix()`), so the rate measures CALL MIX (40-90% across the cohort) and never measured the matcher. Replaced with an ABSOLUTE test -- did the import parser recognise package names as receivers in this repo, >=100 of them -- because the risk a control guards here is a FALSE ZERO. The evidence the old metric was invalid is the twelve read sites and is INDEPENDENT of coredns's result, which is what separates this from rationalising away a failed control.\n\nDECISION TAKEN, overrulable: DO NOT FIX THE EMITTER. Zero measured benefit over 14 repositories, against a real regression surface in a field several consumers read. INSTEAD a dated DECLARED BLINDNESS now sits in go.py's module docstring, where a future predicate-writer will actually encounter it rather than having to know to search the tracker -- it states that the field is a constant on Go, that no predicate may be keyed on it to separate a function row from a method row, that this is deliberate, and what the sizing was. That closes the forward hazard this item correctly identified without paying for a fix that buys nothing.\n\nNOT ESTABLISHED: Go only. The bidirectional function<->method confusion the 2026-08-27 concept audit measured across languages (19,611 function->method edges) is a different population and stays open."  # 1352
